      "level": 1,
      "content": "Unordered Lists: <ul> Tag"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You use the <ul> tag to define an unordered list of items. The <ul> tag requires the <li> tag to define each item in the list."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, <ul> stands for unordered list, and <li> stands for list item."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's create a list of grocery items using these tags."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<ul>\n2    <li>Milk</li>\n3    <li>Bread</li>\n4    <li>Paper Towels</li>\n5    <li>Apples</li>\n6</ul>"
    },
